#ASSERT `s 103(2.1) the punishment in any other case` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited weapon` EQUALS JUST (Punishment WITH `mode` IS `by indictment`, `maximum imprisonment` IS (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`), `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`, `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`, `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`)   -- the object is a prohibited weapon: any other case, not more than 14 years
#ASSERT `s 103(2.1) the punishment in any other case` `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon` EQUALS JUST (Punishment WITH `mode` IS `by indictment`, `maximum imprisonment` IS (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`), `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`, `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`, `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`)   -- the object is a restricted weapon: any other case, not more than 14 years
#ASSERT `s 103(2.1) the punishment in any other case` `s 84(1) kind: a thing that is none of those` EQUALS JUST (Punishment WITH `mode` IS `by indictment`, `maximum imprisonment` IS (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`), `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`, `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`, `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`)   -- the object is a thing that is none of the classes: any other case, not more than 14 years
#ASSERT `s 103(2.1) the punishment in any other case` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the object is a prohibited firearm: subsection (2) governs
#ASSERT `s 103(2.1) the punishment in any other case` `s 84(1) kind: a restricted firearm` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the object is a restricted firearm: subsection (2) governs
#ASSERT `s 103(2.1) the punishment in any other case` `s 84(1) kind: a non-restricted firearm` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the object is a non-restricted firearm: subsection (2) governs
#ASSERT `s 103(2.1) the punishment in any other case` `s 84(1) kind: a replica firearm` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the object is a replica firearm: subsection (2) governs
#ASSERT `s 103(2.1) the punishment in any other case` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited device other than a replica firearm` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the object is a prohibited device other than a replica firearm: subsection (2) governs
#ASSERT `s 103(2.1) the punishment in any other case` `s 84(1) kind: a firearm part` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the object is a firearm part: subsection (2) governs
#ASSERT `s 103(2.1) the punishment in any other case` `s 84(1) kind: prohibited ammunition` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the object is a prohibited ammunition: subsection (2) governs

-- (3) is shown repealed
#ASSERT `s 103(3) as the text shows it` EQUALS "(3) [Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 28]"   -- the text shows "(3) [Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 28]"

§§ `Section 104`

-- `s 104(1) the person commits an offence of unauthorized importing or exporting`
-- inputs, in the order of the GIVEN:
--   1. the kind of thing (`s 84(1) kind of thing`)
--   2. it is a component or part, other than a firearm part, designed exclusively for use in the manufacture of or assembly into an automatic firearm (BOOLEAN)
--   3. s 84(1) import: the act is an import (MAYBE BOOLEAN)
--   4. s 84(1) export: the act is an export (MAYBE BOOLEAN)
--   5. the act is under the authority of the Firearms Act or any other Act of Parliament or any regulations made under an Act of Parliament (BOOLEAN)
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the person commits an offence of unauthorized importing or exporting` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- imports a prohibited firearm otherwise than under the authority of an Act or regulations
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the person commits an offence of unauthorized importing or exporting` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- exports it
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the person commits an offence of unauthorized importing or exporting` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither imports nor exports
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the person commits an offence of unauthorized importing or exporting` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- under the authority of the Firearms Act: "otherwise than under the authority of" limits the prohibition
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the person commits an offence of unauthorized importing or exporting` `s 84(1) kind: a thing that is none of those` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a component or part designed exclusively for an automatic firearm (b)
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the person commits an offence of unauthorized importing or exporting` `s 84(1) kind: ammunition other than prohibited ammunition` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- ordinary ammunition is not named
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the person commits an offence of unauthorized importing or exporting` `s 84(1) kind: a cross-bow` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a cross-bow is not named
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the person commits an offence of unauthorized importing or exporting` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether the act is an import is not covered
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the person commits an offence of unauthorized importing or exporting` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- whether the act is an import is not covered, but the person exports it

-- `s 104(2) the class of the offence`
#ASSERT `s 104(2) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`  -- both indictable and punishable on summary conviction

-- `s 104(2)(a) the punishment on indictment`
#ASSERT `s 104(2)(a) the punishment on indictment` EQUALS (Punishment WITH `mode` IS `by indictment`, `maximum imprisonment` IS (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`, `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`, `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`)   -- the indictable limb

-- `s 104(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction`
-- inputs, in the order of the GIVEN:
--   1. s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction (Punishment)
#ASSERT `s 104(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` `ccc4 test fixture: a stand-in for section 787(1)` EQUALS `ccc4 test fixture: a stand-in for section 787(1)`  -- the limb states no penalty: it returns the answer of section 787(1) given as input (a stand-in value)

-- (3) is shown repealed
#ASSERT `s 104(3) as the text shows it` EQUALS "(3) [Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 29]"   -- the text shows "(3) [Repealed, 2019, c. 25, s. 29]"

§ `Offence Relating to Altering Cartridge Magazine`

§§ `Section 104.1`

-- `s 104.1(1) the person commits an offence of altering a cartridge magazine`
-- inputs, in the order of the GIVEN:
--   1. s 84(1) cartridge magazine: the thing altered is a cartridge magazine (MAYBE BOOLEAN)
--   2. before the alteration it is not a prohibited device (BOOLEAN)
--   3. the person alters it (BOOLEAN)
--   4. s 84(1) prohibited device: after the alteration it is a prohibited device (MAYBE BOOLEAN)
--   5. the person has a lawful excuse (BOOLEAN)
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) the person commits an offence of altering a cartridge magazine` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alters a cartridge magazine that is not a prohibited device so that it becomes one
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) the person commits an offence of altering a cartridge magazine` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- with lawful excuse: "without lawful excuse" limits the prohibition
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) the person commits an offence of altering a cartridge magazine` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the thing is not a cartridge magazine
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) the person commits an offence of altering a cartridge magazine` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the cartridge magazine is already a prohibited device
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) the person commits an offence of altering a cartridge magazine` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- does not alter it
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) the person commits an offence of altering a cartridge magazine` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- after the alteration it is not a prohibited device
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) the person commits an offence of altering a cartridge magazine` NOTHING TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether it is a cartridge magazine is not covered
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) the person commits an offence of altering a cartridge magazine` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether it becomes a prohibited device is not covered
#ASSERT `s 104.1(1) the person commits an offence of altering a cartridge magazine` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- with lawful excuse but no alteration

-- `s 104.1(2) the class of the offence`
#ASSERT `s 104.1(2) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`  -- both indictable and punishable on summary conviction

-- `s 104.1(2)(a) the punishment on indictment`
#ASSERT `s 104.1(2)(a) the punishment on indictment` EQUALS (Punishment WITH `mode` IS `by indictment`, `maximum imprisonment` IS (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`, `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`, `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`)   -- the indictable limb

-- `s 104.1(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction`
-- inputs, in the order of the GIVEN:
--   1. s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction (Punishment)
#ASSERT `s 104.1(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` `ccc4 test fixture: a stand-in for section 787(1)` EQUALS `ccc4 test fixture: a stand-in for section 787(1)`  -- the limb states no penalty: it returns the answer of section 787(1) given as input (a stand-in value)

§ `Offences relating to Lost, Destroyed or Defaced Weapons, etc.`

§§ `Section 105`

-- `s 105(1)(a) the person commits an offence by not reporting a loss`
-- inputs, in the order of the GIVEN:
--   1. the kind of thing (`s 84(1) kind of thing`)
--   2. it is an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate (BOOLEAN)
--   3. the person has lost it, or has had it stolen from the person’s possession (BOOLEAN)
--   4. the person does not with reasonable despatch report the loss to a peace officer, to a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer (BOOLEAN)
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(a) the person commits an offence by not reporting a loss` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- having lost a prohibited firearm, does not with reasonable despatch report the loss
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(a) the person commits an offence by not reporting a loss` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing lost is a prohibited firearm
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(a) the person commits an offence by not reporting a loss` `s 84(1) kind: a restricted firearm` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing lost is a restricted firearm
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(a) the person commits an offence by not reporting a loss` `s 84(1) kind: a non-restricted firearm` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing lost is a non-restricted firearm
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(a) the person commits an offence by not reporting a loss` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited weapon` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing lost is a prohibited weapon
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(a) the person commits an offence by not reporting a loss` `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing lost is a restricted weapon
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(a) the person commits an offence by not reporting a loss` `s 84(1) kind: a replica firearm` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing lost is a replica firearm
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(a) the person commits an offence by not reporting a loss` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited device other than a replica firearm` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing lost is a prohibited device other than a replica firearm
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(a) the person commits an offence by not reporting a loss` `s 84(1) kind: prohibited ammunition` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing lost is a prohibited ammunition
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(a) the person commits an offence by not reporting a loss` `s 84(1) kind: ammunition other than prohibited ammunition` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- ordinary ammunition is not named ("any prohibited ammunition")
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(a) the person commits an offence by not reporting a loss` `s 84(1) kind: a firearm part` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a firearm part is not named
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(a) the person commits an offence by not reporting a loss` `s 84(1) kind: a thing that is none of those` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(a) the person commits an offence by not reporting a loss` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "or having had it stolen from the person’s possession" (the same input)
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(a) the person commits an offence by not reporting a loss` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- has not lost it
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(a) the person commits an offence by not reporting a loss` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- reports the loss with reasonable despatch

-- `s 105(1)(b) the person commits an offence by not delivering or reporting a find`
-- inputs, in the order of the GIVEN:
--   1. the kind of thing (`s 84(1) kind of thing`)
--   2. the person finds it (BOOLEAN)
--   3. the person has reasonable grounds to believe that it has been lost or abandoned (BOOLEAN)
--   4. the person does not with reasonable despatch deliver it to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer or report the finding to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer (BOOLEAN)
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(b) the person commits an offence by not delivering or reporting a find` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- on finding a prohibited firearm believed lost or abandoned, does not with reasonable despatch deliver it or report the finding
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(b) the person commits an offence by not delivering or reporting a find` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing found is a prohibited firearm
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(b) the person commits an offence by not delivering or reporting a find` `s 84(1) kind: a restricted firearm` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing found is a restricted firearm
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(b) the person commits an offence by not delivering or reporting a find` `s 84(1) kind: a non-restricted firearm` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing found is a non-restricted firearm
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(b) the person commits an offence by not delivering or reporting a find` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited weapon` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing found is a prohibited weapon
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(b) the person commits an offence by not delivering or reporting a find` `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing found is a restricted weapon
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(b) the person commits an offence by not delivering or reporting a find` `s 84(1) kind: a replica firearm` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing found is a replica firearm
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(b) the person commits an offence by not delivering or reporting a find` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited device other than a replica firearm` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing found is a prohibited device other than a replica firearm
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(b) the person commits an offence by not delivering or reporting a find` `s 84(1) kind: prohibited ammunition` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing found is a prohibited ammunition
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(b) the person commits an offence by not delivering or reporting a find` `s 84(1) kind: a thing that is none of those` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a licence found is not named in paragraph (b)
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(b) the person commits an offence by not delivering or reporting a find` `s 84(1) kind: ammunition other than prohibited ammunition` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- ordinary ammunition is not named
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(b) the person commits an offence by not delivering or reporting a find` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- does not find it
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(b) the person commits an offence by not delivering or reporting a find` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no reasonable grounds to believe it lost or abandoned
#ASSERT `s 105(1)(b) the person commits an offence by not delivering or reporting a find` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- delivers it or reports the finding with reasonable despatch

-- `s 105(2) the class of the offence`
#ASSERT `s 105(2) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`  -- both indictable and punishable on summary conviction

-- `s 105(2)(a) the punishment on indictment`
#ASSERT `s 105(2)(a) the punishment on indictment` EQUALS (Punishment WITH `mode` IS `by indictment`, `maximum imprisonment` IS (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`, `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`, `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`)   -- the indictable limb

-- `s 105(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction`
-- inputs, in the order of the GIVEN:
--   1. s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction (Punishment)
#ASSERT `s 105(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` `ccc4 test fixture: a stand-in for section 787(1)` EQUALS `ccc4 test fixture: a stand-in for section 787(1)`  -- the limb states no penalty: it returns the answer of section 787(1) given as input (a stand-in value)

§§ `Section 106`

-- `s 106(1) the person commits an offence by not reporting a destruction`
-- inputs, in the order of the GIVEN:
--   1. the kind of thing (`s 84(1) kind of thing`)
--   2. the person has destroyed it (BOOLEAN)
--   3. the person has become aware of the destruction of it, and it was in the person’s possession before its destruction (BOOLEAN)
--   4. the person does not with reasonable despatch report the destruction to a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer (BOOLEAN)
#ASSERT `s 106(1) the person commits an offence by not reporting a destruction` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a) after destroying a prohibited firearm, does not with reasonable despatch report the destruction
#ASSERT `s 106(1) the person commits an offence by not reporting a destruction` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) on becoming aware of the destruction of one that was in the person’s possession
#ASSERT `s 106(1) the person commits an offence by not reporting a destruction` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither destroyed nor aware of a destruction
#ASSERT `s 106(1) the person commits an offence by not reporting a destruction` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- reports the destruction with reasonable despatch
#ASSERT `s 106(1) the person commits an offence by not reporting a destruction` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing is a prohibited firearm
#ASSERT `s 106(1) the person commits an offence by not reporting a destruction` `s 84(1) kind: a restricted firearm` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing is a restricted firearm
#ASSERT `s 106(1) the person commits an offence by not reporting a destruction` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited weapon` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing is a prohibited weapon
#ASSERT `s 106(1) the person commits an offence by not reporting a destruction` `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing is a restricted weapon
#ASSERT `s 106(1) the person commits an offence by not reporting a destruction` `s 84(1) kind: a replica firearm` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing is a replica firearm
#ASSERT `s 106(1) the person commits an offence by not reporting a destruction` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited device other than a replica firearm` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing is a prohibited device other than a replica firearm
#ASSERT `s 106(1) the person commits an offence by not reporting a destruction` `s 84(1) kind: prohibited ammunition` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the thing is a prohibited ammunition
#ASSERT `s 106(1) the person commits an offence by not reporting a destruction` `s 84(1) kind: a non-restricted firearm` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a non-restricted firearm is not named in this subsection
#ASSERT `s 106(1) the person commits an offence by not reporting a destruction` `s 84(1) kind: ammunition other than prohibited ammunition` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- ordinary ammunition is not named
#ASSERT `s 106(1) the person commits an offence by not reporting a destruction` `s 84(1) kind: a firearm part` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a firearm part is not named

-- `s 106(2) the class of the offence`
#ASSERT `s 106(2) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`  -- both indictable and punishable on summary conviction

-- `s 106(2)(a) the punishment on indictment`
#ASSERT `s 106(2)(a) the punishment on indictment` EQUALS (Punishment WITH `mode` IS `by indictment`, `maximum imprisonment` IS (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`, `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`, `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`)   -- the indictable limb

-- `s 106(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction`
-- inputs, in the order of the GIVEN:
--   1. s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction (Punishment)
#ASSERT `s 106(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` `ccc4 test fixture: a stand-in for section 787(1)` EQUALS `ccc4 test fixture: a stand-in for section 787(1)`  -- the limb states no penalty: it returns the answer of section 787(1) given as input (a stand-in value)

§§ `Section 107`

-- `s 107(1) the person commits an offence by making a false report or statement`
-- inputs, in the order of the GIVEN:
--   1. the kind of thing (`s 84(1) kind of thing`)
--   2. it is an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate (BOOLEAN)
--   3. the person makes a report or statement before a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer (BOOLEAN)
--   4. the report or statement concerns the loss, theft or destruction of it (BOOLEAN)
--   5. the report or statement is false (BOOLEAN)
--   6. the person makes it knowingly (BOOLEAN)
#ASSERT `s 107(1) the person commits an offence by making a false report or statement` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- knowingly makes, before a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer, a false report concerning the loss, theft or destruction of a prohibited firearm
#ASSERT `s 107(1) the person commits an offence by making a false report or statement` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- concerning a prohibited firearm
#ASSERT `s 107(1) the person commits an offence by making a false report or statement` `s 84(1) kind: a restricted firearm` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- concerning a restricted firearm
#ASSERT `s 107(1) the person commits an offence by making a false report or statement` `s 84(1) kind: a non-restricted firearm` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- concerning a non-restricted firearm
#ASSERT `s 107(1) the person commits an offence by making a false report or statement` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited weapon` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- concerning a prohibited weapon
#ASSERT `s 107(1) the person commits an offence by making a false report or statement` `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- concerning a restricted weapon
#ASSERT `s 107(1) the person commits an offence by making a false report or statement` `s 84(1) kind: a replica firearm` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- concerning a replica firearm
#ASSERT `s 107(1) the person commits an offence by making a false report or statement` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited device other than a replica firearm` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- concerning a prohibited device other than a replica firearm
#ASSERT `s 107(1) the person commits an offence by making a false report or statement` `s 84(1) kind: prohibited ammunition` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- concerning a prohibited ammunition
#ASSERT `s 107(1) the person commits an offence by making a false report or statement` `s 84(1) kind: a thing that is none of those` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- concerning an authorization, a licence or a registration certificate
#ASSERT `s 107(1) the person commits an offence by making a false report or statement` `s 84(1) kind: ammunition other than prohibited ammunition` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- ordinary ammunition is not named
#ASSERT `s 107(1) the person commits an offence by making a false report or statement` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not made before a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer
#ASSERT `s 107(1) the person commits an offence by making a false report or statement` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not concerning loss, theft or destruction
#ASSERT `s 107(1) the person commits an offence by making a false report or statement` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the report is true
#ASSERT `s 107(1) the person commits an offence by making a false report or statement` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not made knowingly

-- `s 107(2) the class of the offence`
#ASSERT `s 107(2) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`  -- both indictable and punishable on summary conviction

-- `s 107(2)(a) the punishment on indictment`
#ASSERT `s 107(2)(a) the punishment on indictment` EQUALS (Punishment WITH `mode` IS `by indictment`, `maximum imprisonment` IS (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`, `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`, `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`)   -- the indictable limb

-- `s 107(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction`
-- inputs, in the order of the GIVEN:
--   1. s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction (Punishment)
#ASSERT `s 107(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` `ccc4 test fixture: a stand-in for section 787(1)` EQUALS `ccc4 test fixture: a stand-in for section 787(1)`  -- the limb states no penalty: it returns the answer of section 787(1) given as input (a stand-in value)

-- `s 107(3) report or statement`
-- inputs, in the order of the GIVEN:
--   1. the assertion (`s 107(3) assertion`)
#ASSERT `s 107(3) report or statement` `s 107(3) assertion: of fact` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an assertion of fact
#ASSERT `s 107(3) report or statement` `s 107(3) assertion: of opinion` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an assertion of opinion
#ASSERT `s 107(3) report or statement` `s 107(3) assertion: of belief` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an assertion of belief
#ASSERT `s 107(3) report or statement` `s 107(3) assertion: of knowledge` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an assertion of knowledge
#ASSERT `s 107(3) report or statement` `s 107(3) assertion: a thing that is none of those` EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a thing that is none of those: "means" is closed

§§ `Section 108`

-- `s 108(1) the person commits an offence of tampering with a serial number`
-- inputs, in the order of the GIVEN:
--   1. the kind of thing (`s 84(1) kind of thing`)
--   2. the person alters, defaces or removes a serial number on it (BOOLEAN)
--   3. the person possesses it knowing that the serial number on it has been altered, defaced or removed (BOOLEAN)
--   4. the person has a lawful excuse (BOOLEAN)
#ASSERT `s 108(1) the person commits an offence of tampering with a serial number` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a) alters, defaces or removes a serial number on a firearm
#ASSERT `s 108(1) the person commits an offence of tampering with a serial number` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) possesses a firearm knowing that the serial number on it has been altered, defaced or removed
#ASSERT `s 108(1) the person commits an offence of tampering with a serial number` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither
#ASSERT `s 108(1) the person commits an offence of tampering with a serial number` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- with lawful excuse: "without lawful excuse" limits the prohibition
#ASSERT `s 108(1) the person commits an offence of tampering with a serial number` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- with lawful excuse, doing neither
#ASSERT `s 108(1) the person commits an offence of tampering with a serial number` `s 84(1) kind: a non-restricted firearm` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a non-restricted firearm
#ASSERT `s 108(1) the person commits an offence of tampering with a serial number` `s 84(1) kind: a restricted firearm` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a restricted firearm
#ASSERT `s 108(1) the person commits an offence of tampering with a serial number` `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a restricted weapon is not a firearm
#ASSERT `s 108(1) the person commits an offence of tampering with a serial number` `s 84(1) kind: a replica firearm` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a replica firearm is not a firearm

-- `s 108(2) the class of the offence`
#ASSERT `s 108(2) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`  -- both indictable and punishable on summary conviction

-- `s 108(2)(a) the punishment on indictment`
#ASSERT `s 108(2)(a) the punishment on indictment` EQUALS (Punishment WITH `mode` IS `by indictment`, `maximum imprisonment` IS (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`, `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`, `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`)   -- the indictable limb

-- `s 108(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction`
-- inputs, in the order of the GIVEN:
--   1. s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction (Punishment)
#ASSERT `s 108(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` `ccc4 test fixture: a stand-in for section 787(1)` EQUALS `ccc4 test fixture: a stand-in for section 787(1)`  -- the limb states no penalty: it returns the answer of section 787(1) given as input (a stand-in value)

-- `s 108(3) no person is guilty of an offence under paragraph (1)(b) by reason only of possessing the firearm`
-- inputs, in the order of the GIVEN:
--   1. the kind of thing (`s 84(1) kind of thing`)
--   2. the serial number has been replaced (BOOLEAN)
--   3. a registration certificate in respect of the firearm has been issued setting out a new serial number for the firearm (BOOLEAN)
#ASSERT `s 108(3) no person is guilty of an offence under paragraph (1)(b) by reason only of possessing the firearm` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a prohibited firearm whose serial number has been replaced and a registration certificate setting out the new number has been issued
#ASSERT `s 108(3) no person is guilty of an offence under paragraph (1)(b) by reason only of possessing the firearm` `s 84(1) kind: a restricted firearm` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a restricted firearm in the same case
#ASSERT `s 108(3) no person is guilty of an offence under paragraph (1)(b) by reason only of possessing the firearm` `s 84(1) kind: a non-restricted firearm` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a non-restricted firearm: the subsection names only prohibited and restricted firearms
#ASSERT `s 108(3) no person is guilty of an offence under paragraph (1)(b) by reason only of possessing the firearm` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the serial number has not been replaced
#ASSERT `s 108(3) no person is guilty of an offence under paragraph (1)(b) by reason only of possessing the firearm` `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no registration certificate setting out the new number has been issued

-- `s 108(4) the evidence is proof that the person possesses the firearm knowing that the serial number on it has been altered, defaced or removed`
-- inputs, in the order of the GIVEN:
--   1. the person possesses the firearm (BOOLEAN)
--   2. the serial number on it has been wholly or partially obliterated otherwise than through normal use over time (BOOLEAN)
--   3. there is evidence to the contrary (BOOLEAN)
#ASSERT `s 108(4) the evidence is proof that the person possesses the firearm knowing that the serial number on it has been altered, defaced or removed` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- evidence of possession of a firearm with a serial number obliterated otherwise than through normal use, and no evidence to the contrary
#ASSERT `s 108(4) the evidence is proof that the person possesses the firearm knowing that the serial number on it has been altered, defaced or removed` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "in the absence of evidence to the contrary": there is such evidence
#ASSERT `s 108(4) the evidence is proof that the person possesses the firearm knowing that the serial number on it has been altered, defaced or removed` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the serial number is not obliterated otherwise than through normal use over time
#ASSERT `s 108(4) the evidence is proof that the person possesses the firearm knowing that the serial number on it has been altered, defaced or removed` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the person does not possess the firearm

§ `The duties of sections 105 and 106, as regulative rules (#TRACE; a deontic value cannot be asserted on the stable binary, see NOTES.md)`

-- The person bound is `the accused`; the text fixes no period, so the rules have no WITHIN.  A trace holding the act ends FULFILLED; a trace without it leaves the duty standing.
#TRACE `s 105(1)(a) the duty to report a loss` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 105 report the loss to a peace officer, to a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer` AT 3

#TRACE `s 105(1)(a) the duty to report a loss` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

#TRACE `s 105(1)(b) the duty to deliver or report a find` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 105 deliver the found thing to a peace officer, a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer, or report the finding to one of them` AT 3

#TRACE `s 105(1)(b) the duty to deliver or report a find` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

#TRACE `s 106(1) the duty to report a destruction` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 106 report the destruction to a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer` AT 3

#TRACE `s 106(1) the duty to report a destruction` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

-- the wrong act (a report of a loss does not discharge the duty to report a destruction): the duty stays standing
#TRACE `s 106(1) the duty to report a destruction` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 105 report the loss to a peace officer, to a firearms officer or a chief firearms officer` AT 3

